    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "· The Bolide Bag ·",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The history of the Hermès Bolide dates back to 1923, making it the world's first handbag with a zipper closure. Originally named \"le sac pour l'auto\"—meaning \"car bag\"—because its zipper was inspired by the Ford automobile factory, it was later renamed \"Bolide,\" which means \"comet\" and also pays tribute to the rapidly growing automotive industry of the time.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/6nw97hu/b58a3a6a2826c63d.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/6nw97hu/872b678adde50d46.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The bag features an architectural shell-like silhouette with a top zip closure, while its flat base and metal feet allow it to stand upright stably, with a spacious interior. Thanks to its clean lines and practical functionality, the Bolide became an ideal travel companion for adventurers as soon as it was launched.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/6nw97hu/367e569aff9d62ba.jpg",
